// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Shadow Trading v1
//
// Specification: docs/trading/03-domain-model.md and docs/trading/04-state-machines.md.
// Additive only. The legacy PaperAccount / PaperOrder / PaperPosition models and
// the PaperSignalEvaluation research model stay untouched (ADR 0002).
//
// Modelling rules (docs/trading/03, "Modellierungsregeln"):
//   - money, price, quantity, rate and P&L are Decimal(30,12), never Float;
//   - percentages are decimal rates, basis points are Int inside versioned profiles;
//   - all timestamps are UTC; daily limits additionally carry tradingDateUtc;
//   - financial history deletes with Restrict — no cascade from portfolio,
//     strategy version, candidate, order, fill, position or audit;
//   - evidence, fills, ledger, position events and audit rows are append-only.
//
// "At most one active row per scope" is expressed by a nullable unique key
// column (PostgreSQL treats NULL as distinct), because Prisma cannot declare a
// partial unique index. The domain package builds those keys.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

enum StrategyStatus {
  DRAFT
  ACTIVE
  RETIRED
}

enum StrategyVersionStatus {
  DRAFT
  APPROVED
  ACTIVE
  RETIRED
}

enum TradeDirection {
